  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "When \\(x\\) is added to both the numerator and the denominator of the fraction \\(\\frac{a}{b},\\) \\(a\\ne b,\\) \\(b\\ne0,\\) the value of the fraction is changed to \\(\\frac{c}{d}.\\) Then \\(x\\) equals:",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac1{c-d}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac{ad-bc}{c-d}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac{ad-bc}{c+d}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac{bc-ad}{c-d}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac{bc-ad}{c+d}\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "b",
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1969-p1.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "From \\[ \\frac{a+x}{b+x}=\\frac cd \\] we obtain \\(ad+dx=bc+cx.\\) Hence \\(x(d-c)=bc-ad,\\) so \\[ x=\\frac{bc-ad}{d-c}=\\frac{ad-bc}{c-d}. \\]\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is B.",
      "hints": [
        "Translate the change into \\(\\frac{a+x}{b+x}=\\frac{c}{d}\\)",
        "Cross-multiply and collect the terms containing \\(x\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
